3. Why it does not work?
```
Status PTSelectStmt::Analyze(SemContext *sem_context) {
...
  // Find the optimal scan path.
  if (is_top_level_) {
...
    // Analyze column references and available indexes to find the best scan path.
    // Save the optimal scan-path to scan spec.
    RETURN_NOT_OK(AnalyzeIndexes(sem_context, &scan_spec));   <<< USED partition_key_ops_ !
...
  }

  // Run error checking on the WHERE conditions.
  RETURN_NOT_OK(AnalyzeWhereClause(sem_context));   <<< INIT partition_key_ops_ !
```
So, `partition_key_ops_` is initialized AFTER it was used by `AnalyzeIndexes`.
4. How we call once again WHERE-expression Analyze(), but it does not help:
```
Status PTSelectStmt::Analyze(SemContext *sem_context) {
...
